# AICL Example: Flight Booking System
# A comprehensive flight booking system with search and booking, seat management,
# dynamic pricing, check-in processing, baggage management, and loyalty program
# Demonstrates ALL 10 AICL language levels

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 1 — Architecture (Mandatory)
# =============================================================================

Goal:
Create a flight booking system that supports flight search and reservation, seat allocation and management, dynamic fare pricing, online check-in, baggage tracking, loyalty program integration, and multi-airline code sharing

Constraint:
Flight search must return results within 3 seconds

Constraint:
Booking confirmation must be atomic and idempotent

Constraint:
System must support at least 20000 concurrent booking sessions

Constraint:
All passenger data must comply with GDPR and aviation data protection regulations

Constraint:
Pricing must be synchronized with airline revenue management systems within 30 seconds

Constraint:
Check-in window must open exactly 24 hours before departure

Risk:
Overbooking leads to denied boarding

Recovery:
Offer voluntary rebooking with compensation and rebook on next available flight

Risk:
Payment authorization fails during booking

Recovery:
Hold reservation for 15 minutes and retry payment and alert customer

Risk:
Flight cancellation or significant delay

Recovery:
Automatically rebook affected passengers and issue compensation per EU261 or DOT rules

Risk:
Seat allocation conflict on fully booked flight

Recovery:
Reassign seats using priority rules and notify affected passengers

Risk:
Loyalty point calculation discrepancy

Recovery:
Recalculate from transaction log and credit difference and audit point system

Risk:
System overload during flash sale or holiday peak

Recovery:
Enable virtual waiting room and scale capacity and prioritize in-progress bookings

Layer:
Search and Discovery
